    "created_at": "2024-12-19T17:21:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-19T17:21:39Z",
    "body": "Quoting @johannhof in https://github.com/WICG/cookie-store/issues/91#issuecomment-2545886898\r\n> A better title for this section may have been \"Don't use cookies as an arbitrary key-value store in your application\",\r\n\r\nYes, this was the heart of my original concern, especially since at the time the ServiceWorkers WG was seeing a lot of requests that were very much along the lines of requesting access to LocalStorage (and all of the performance problems that could entail but which are largely hidden from users/developers) or potentially unlimited data storage directly on the registration in a structured serialization record (which could have similar performance problems).\r\n\r\nIt also seemed like https://github.com/WICG/kv-storage was on a viable path to standardization and implementation at that time.  My understanding of the rough consensus of the evolution of that is that we should simply be enhancing IndexedDB to also have a more ergonomic shape along the lines of kv-storage or https://github.com/jakearchibald/idb and I think we are indeed moving that direction once again.\r\n\r\nWhich is to say, I think the answer to \"what should I use for key-value storage in my ServiceWorker\" is IndexedDB and we can probably close this.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
